<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;only&nbsp;my&nbsp;second&nbsp;critique&nbsp;ever</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;never&nbsp;mind</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I start out with the disclaimer that I'm new to the site and don't know if this has been done before or not.</p>
<p>I've seen at least one example of a trip into an alternate reality. I'm thinking of <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-093" target="_blank">SCP-093</a>.</p>
<p>Since it's an SCP article written from the perspective of our reality, there's a physical object that requires containment here while the reality that it allows access to - and the resulting story - takes place in an another dimension.</p>
<p>This raises a fun possibility.</p>
<ul>
<li>SCP team uses anomalous object here in Reality 1 that gives access to a another reality (Reality 2)</li>
<li>Team discovers ruins of an SCP Facility in Reality 2 and concludes that their containment of the same object has failed leading to a breach (releasing a virulent parasite) and resulting in this ruined state</li>
<li>Through reading the SCP logs of the researchers in Reality 2 they discover that the site was using a system of trial and error to complete containment procedures</li>
<li>They realize the the failed containment procedure in Reality 2 is the same procedure that they're using in reality 1. They know that they need to change their procedure but they don't know what the next method to try should be.</li>
<li>So, they use the Reality 2 version of the same anomalous object to go to Reality 3 where they find yet another destroyed SCP facility and another failed containment strategy. They learn what failed there.</li>
<li>And so on through a series of nested realities until you decide to bring it to resolution.</li>
</ul>
<p>Story could be told in retrospect through a series of memos. Each from different realities detailing their failure and demise. If you start with memos from the first failed reality and go through to the last you can tell a story of each vain attempt and how the containment becomes more sophisticated over time. Ending with this reality's version of the containment strategy.</p>
</div>
</div>
