			<div class="content" id="post-content-4860152">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>My, core concern with this pitch is that every part of this feels like it's from <a href="/scp-2935">SCP-2935</a>, with the exception of the cause of death being explicitly a parasite here.</p>
<p>Moving beyond this, I have a number of questions:</p>
<ul>
<li>What actually is the SCP beyond 'a parasite'?
<ul>
<li>What makes it anomalous?</li>
<li>What does it actually do? Like it makes someone 'sick' but how does this manifest?</li>
<li>Is the parasite what ruined the foundation?</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>How did the SCP Foundation get the video logs?
<ul>
<li>I'm asking because the person is implied to not be in the Foundation; and they're also not in the Foundation's reality</li>
<li>On a related note: why did the person make video logs?</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>What's in the alternate universe? Is it empty? Is it all ruined? Is it just the Foundation that's ruined and everything else is okay?</li>
</ul>
<p>My, central concern is that at the moment it feels like this really needs more fleshing out before anyone can really offer any useful advice here: there's definitely good ideas in here but it'll be worth really thinking about how you can execute on them, and what you want to do with this. There's definitely good horror in someone slowly dying from a parasite and trying to do their best to like survive, but this just&#8230;really needs you to figure out the plot beats that happen as this occurs: how do they try to survive? What do they experience as they try to survive? Do they succeed or fail?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

