			<div class="content" id="post-content-4861606">
									

<p><strong>Summoned via PM:</strong></p>
<p>Hi there Emily123456789. Let’s explore your concept.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the SCP is a parasite that slowly suffocates you and also slowly drives you insane because you never get used to the parasite in your airways</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If you’re going with this as your main anomaly, tell us more about it. What is its origin? Is it an alien life-form? Was it created in a lab somewhere? What are the parasite’s capabilities / goals? Why does it, for example, “slowly suffocate you” AND “drive you insane”? How are these two anomalous effects related?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the video logs are set in an alternate universe where this person stumbles upon the ruins of the foundation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>While interesting, this statement raises more questions as well. Why is there “an alternate universe”? How did the Foundation access this? Who is this “person” in the first place who stumbles upon these logs? Tell us more about who we’re following and why he/she is significant?</p>
<p>As <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5336470&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609733802" alt="cybersqyd" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5336470)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;">cybersqyd</a></span> has said, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2935">SCP-2935</a> also features an end-of-the-world-by-disease scenario but from a unique perspective of a sole survivor who also turns out to be the catalyst of the plague. Or you could go the route of <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3519">SCP-3519</a> which is more a broad overview of events transpiring. The backdrop can be a world-ending disease, but what’s your own unique spin on the narrative?</p>
<p>Overall, it feels like there are many starting points from which you can expand and branch off further. Your job is to either elaborate on each of these components in order to connect them all into a coherent narrative, OR cut some of these anomalous effects out if they don’t fit in the end.</p>
<p>If you decide to revise the concept / respond below, do drop me another PM and I’ll take another look. Best of luck for now!</p>

